title: ninja_village_context
---
// The Ninja Village's conversations (gate address SILENT), one node per
// resident, named `ninja_village_<resident>`. The rooms are written by
// `tools/ambition_ldtk_tools/specs/ninja_village/make_specs.py`.
//
// The village's training beat: the dojo's rank exam, the encounter
// `ninja_village.rank_exam` (the dummies, then the examiner). Reporting to
// the teacher after it sets `ninja_village_rank_awarded`; the quest
// `ninja_village_rank_exam` pays the reward.
//
// Never played. No placement names this node; it declares the zone.
===

title: ninja_village_sato
---
Sato: Good morning. The ring is swept. The leaves are not. They never will be.
-> Do many come through the gate?
    Sato: Couriers, pilgrims, merchants. Some bow to the ring. Most of them are only dizzy.
-> Is the ring sacred?
    Sato: It is old, it is useful, and people are grateful for it. Here that is close enough. I sweep round it as I sweep round the stones.
-> Do you know Kagero?
    Sato: The one with the white scarf? Only by reputation. Hayashi says she works alone.
    Sato: People mention her when they talk about the castle. They usually lower their voices.
-> Good morning.
===

title: ninja_village_nagisa
---
Nagisa: *tok, tok* Welcome through the SILENT gate. I am Nagisa. I keep it.
-> What does a gatekeeper do?
    Nagisa: I listen to the ring. Everything that crosses makes a sound. Couriers sound like a sigh. Trouble sounds like nothing at all.
    Nagisa: Sato keeps the stones clean. I keep the ring honest.
-> Why is the gate called SILENT?
    Nagisa: A ninja village does not announce itself. Its address should not either.
-> What brings an alligator to a mountain village?
    Nagisa: A river, once. Then the gate. A gate wants someone patient at the door, and nobody waits like a gator.
-> Has anything strange come through?
    Nagisa: Kenji's letters to the castle side. They go out, and the ring brings them back unopened.
    Nagisa: A gate does not refuse the post. Someone on the other side refuses it for the gate.
-> Thank you.
===

title: ninja_village_kenji
---
Kenji: Do not sit too near. I came through the ring an hour ago and the ground is still deciding.
-> Is the gate always like this?
    Kenji: Every time. The letters arrive perfectly. The courier arrives green.
-> Why not take the mountain road?
    Kenji: Four days. The village wants its post today. My stomach has filed a complaint with the post office.
-> Anything worrying in the post?
    Kenji: Three letters sent toward the castle side came back unopened. Same handwriting on the back of every one.
    Kenji: The woman who wrote them asked me to try again tomorrow. I said I would.
-> Feel better.
===

title: ninja_village_ume
---
Ume: Welcome. Tea for the tired, and for the gate-sick at half price. You do not look gate-sick.
-> Why do people run on the roofs?
    Ume: It is quicker than the street, and the dojo marks you for it. After the rice is in, the whole village is up there.
-> Tell me about the dojo.
    Ume: Sensei Hayashi runs a rank exam on the hour. Daichi has failed it eleven times. He is very proud of the number.
-> Can anyone get a room here?
    Ume: I've got two upstairs. One family paid ahead and left before daylight. The little one forgot her shoes.
    Ume: If they come back, they're under the bed. I'm leaving them there.
-> Do the students eat here?
    Ume: Daichi eats like he's won the exam. Ren eats standing up. Hayashi brings his own rice and borrows my salt.
-> Thank you.
===

title: ninja_village_daichi
---
Daichi: Stand back! I am about to perform the Thousand Leaf Step! ...I am still learning the name of the second part.
-> What is the rank exam?
    Daichi: Part one, the dummies. Part two, the examiner. Part three, the forms. I have never seen part three.
-> Why do you shout the moves?
    Daichi: How else will anyone know it was a move? A move nobody hears is just exercise.
-> Have you seen Kagero fight?
    Daichi: No. Ren says she hunts spirits and never announces her moves.
    Daichi: I practiced fighting without shouting yesterday. I fell off a roof. Nobody came to watch.
-> Good luck.
    Daichi: I do not need luck! I need the exam to be on a Tuesday.
===

title: ninja_village_moriyama
---
Moriyama: Downwind of the kiln, please. You are standing in my smoke and I am standing in it for a living.
-> What are you burning?
    Moriyama: Cedar, three days and three nights, with the door shut. What comes out is charcoal. What goes in is patience.
    Moriyama: The tea house cooks on it. The smith forges on it. The dojo heats its bath on it and says it is training.
-> Do ninja pass by here?
    Moriyama: Every one in the clan, sooner or later, sneaking. I see them all. Then they smell of my smoke for a week and everyone else sees them too.
    Moriyama: The Shadow Clan's elders call it the charcoal exam. They did not ask me if they could.
-> Is there anything up in the branches?
    Moriyama: The crows keep what they find on the fourth branch. Coins, mostly. A spoon. They will not miss it as much as they say.
-> I'll leave you to it.
    Moriyama: Leave by the windward side.
===

title: ninja_village_hayashi
---
<<if condition("world.flag_set", "ninja_village_rank_awarded")>>
Sensei Hayashi: The new rank wears well. Do not let it make you slow.
-> What comes after this rank?
    Sensei Hayashi: The next one. It has more forms.
-> What do the ranks mean outside the village?
    Sensei Hayashi: Not much. Wear yours here. Beyond the gate, you'll have to introduce yourself.
-> Thank you, Sensei.
<<elseif condition("encounter.cleared", "ninja_village.rank_exam")>>
Sensei Hayashi: The dummies are broken and the examiner is resting. That is a pass.
-> Accept the rank.
    <<command "world.set_flag" "ninja_village_rank_awarded" true>>
    Sensei Hayashi: Stamped, counter-stamped, and filed. Ren will want to make you her rival. Please let her. It saves time.
-> Not yet.
    Sensei Hayashi: The stamp will wait. The stamp has great patience.
<<else>>
Sensei Hayashi: Welcome to the village dojo. You came to take the rank exam. Everyone who comes in that door came to take the rank exam.
-> How does the exam work?
    Sensei Hayashi: Walk onto the exam floor. Part one: break the dummies. Part two: the examiner. If you lose, ring the bell and begin again. There is no shame in the bell.
-> Can a robot take it?
    Sensei Hayashi: The form says "applicant". It does not say "person". I checked.
-> Does Kagero train here?
    Sensei Hayashi: No. I've seen what she does with a paper talisman. I wouldn't know where to begin teaching it.
-> Later.
<<endif>>
===

title: ninja_village_ren
---
<<if condition("world.flag_set", "ninja_village_rank_awarded")>>
Ren: So you passed. Then it is decided: from today you are my rival. I have the form here. Sign it.
-> Sign the rival form.
    Ren: Good. Next week I will choose a new rival. Do not take it personally. Take it seriously.
-> I don't want a rival.
    Ren: Nobody wants one. That is why the form exists.
-> Why did you pick me?
    Ren: You went through the dummies without stopping to bow to them. I would have stopped. It annoyed me.
<<else>>
Ren: You want to take the exam? Fine. Do not expect me to cheer. I only cheer for rivals.
-> How do I become your rival?
    Ren: Pass the exam. Then I will declare it. There is a form.
-> Any advice?
    Ren: The examiner waits for you to swing first. So do I.
-> Why do you want a rival?
    Ren: Daichi cheers when I land a hit. I'd rather somebody hit me back.
-> Later.
<<endif>>
===
